@startuml student-intake
title Use: a student builds a comparable profile (v2)

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Student
participant "Guided intake UI" as ui
participant "Extractors\n(CV / LinkedIn / GitHub)" as ext
participant "Archetype Router" as router
participant "Completeness model" as comp
database "candidates · profiles\n· evidence" as store

Student -> ui : start profile (upload thin CV if any)
ui -> ext : auto-extract whatever exists
ext --> ui : pre-filled draft (education, projects, links)
ui -> router : confirm STUDENT archetype

== Guided form: ask for what a student CV usually omits ==
ui -> Student : Education detail\n(program, specialization, year/expected graduation, key courses)
ui -> Student : Thesis / final work\n(topic, methods, tools, abstract)
ui -> Student : Projects (school / personal / hackathon)\n(role, tech, link, outcome, team size)
ui -> Student : Internships / part-time\n(incl. off-field — for transferable skills)
ui -> Student : Extracurriculars\n(clubs, competitions, open-source, tutoring)
ui -> Student : Certifications / online courses
ui -> Student : Aspirations & preferences\n(target roles, interests, willingness to learn,\nlocation/remote, availability, languages)
ui -> Student : Self-rated skills\n(explicitly marked self-declared)

loop each captured item
  ui -> comp : update field
  comp --> ui : completeness % + "biggest missing signal" nudge
end

Student -> ui : submit
ui -> store : persist student profile + evidence\n(each item tagged with provenance)

note over ui, comp
  Inversion of BAU: instead of mining a rich CV,
  we *guide* the student to surface signals the
  pipeline can use, and we prioritise links/artifacts
  (GitHub, demo, thesis) over self-rated levels because
  they are verifiable. Completeness drives the ask order.
end note
@enduml
